<title>NORWAY: Norway Sept CPI rises 0.5 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Norway Sept CPI rises 0.5 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Norway issued the following economic indicator.</p>
<p>NORWAY CONSUMER PRICES   SEPT 1996   AUG 1996   SEPT 1995</p>
<p>Figures in percent</p>
<p>  Month-on-month change	0.5	 -0.1	  +0.6</p>
<p>  Year-on-year change	  1.3	 +1.5	  +2.3</p>
<p>  Index (base 1979)	  264.9	263.7	 261.4</p>
<p>NOTE -- Ten economists forecast a year-on-year rise in September of 1.4 percent.  </p>
<p>The Statistics office attributed the 0.5 percent month-on-month rise mainly to higher electricity prices and to an increase in prices on clothes following sales in July and August.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
